---
/**
 * Privacy policy — public page required by the Intuit production review,
 * Google's restricted-scope (Gmail) verification, and Xero certification.
 * The Google Limited Use disclosure below is mandatory wording — do not
 * remove it.
 */
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Privacy Policy · Pocket Ops</title>
  </head>
  <body class="min-h-screen bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-900">
    <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-6 p-6 pb-16">
      <header class="pt-6">
        <a href="/" class="text-sm text-zinc-500 hover:text-zinc-700">← Pocket Ops</a>
        <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-zinc-500">Effective 6 July 2026</p>
      </header>

      <section class="space-y-3 rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Who we are</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-700">
          Pocket Ops is a customer-management and invoicing platform for UK field-service
          businesses. When a trade business ("workspace owner") uses Pocket Ops to manage its
          customers, the workspace owner is the data controller for its customer records and
          Pocket Ops is the data processor. Contact: <a href="mailto:support@pocketops.io" class="underline">support@pocketops.io</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">What we collect</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-700">
          <li><strong>Account data</strong> — your name, email, business details, and a securely hashed password.</li>
          <li><strong>Business records</strong> — customers, jobs, quotes, invoices, payments, photos, expenses, time entries, certificates, and documents you upload.</li>
          <li><strong>Communications</strong> — SMS and email messages between your business and its customers, when you connect a phone number or mailbox.</li>
          <li><strong>Technical data</strong> — IP addresses and security logs used to protect accounts.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">How we use it</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-700">
          Solely to provide the service: running your CRM, sending quotes and invoices, taking
          payments, routing calls and messages, generating documents, and syncing invoices to
          your accounting software. We do not sell personal data, and we do not use your data
          for advertising.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Connected services</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-700">
          Data is shared with these processors only as needed to run features you use:
          Cloudflare (hosting and storage), Stripe (payments — card details go directly to
          Stripe and never touch our servers), Twilio (calls and SMS), Google and Microsoft
          (email, if you connect a mailbox), and Intuit QuickBooks or Xero (accounting, if you
          connect your books). Each connection is made by you and can be disconnected by you
          in Settings at any time, which revokes our access.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-700">
          <strong>Google user data:</strong> Pocket Ops's use and transfer of information
          received from Google APIs adheres to the
          <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" class="underline" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
          including the Limited Use requirements. Gmail data is used only to display and send
          your business email within your inbox; it is never used for advertising, never sold,
          and never read by humans except with your explicit permission for support.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Storage, retention, and your rights</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-700">
          Data is stored with Cloudflare in the European region. We keep your data while your
          workspace is active and delete it on verified request when you close your account,
          except where law requires longer retention (e.g. financial records). Under UK GDPR
          you can request access, correction, deletion, or portability of your personal data,
          and you can complain to the ICO. Customers of a trade business should direct
          requests to that business (the controller); we assist them in fulfilling requests.
        </p>
      </section>

      <footer class="text-center text-xs text-zinc-400">
        <a href="/terms" class="underline">Terms of Service</a> · © 2026 Pocket Ops
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
